---
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<section class="ab-board" id="board">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="ab-board-header">
      <div class="eyebrow ctr" style="margin-bottom: 14px">Leadership</div>
      <h2>Board of <span class="red">Directors</span></h2>
      <p>The people who show up every day to make sure Alabama's veterans are never left behind.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="ab-board-grid">
      <div class="ab-member">
        <img
          src="https://alabamaveteran.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/chris-montz.webp"
          alt="Chris Montz"
          class="ab-member-photo"
        />
        <div class="ab-member-role">President</div>
        <div class="ab-member-name">Chris Montz</div>
        <div class="ab-member-title">Sr. Loan Officer · Edge Home Finance</div>
        <p class="ab-member-bio">
          A founding board member since 2017, Chris comes from a family of veterans and has spent
          over two decades specializing in VA home loans. He leads Alabama Veteran with a personal
          mission rooted in honor, service, and the belief that no veteran should navigate civilian
          life alone.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="ab-member">
        <img
          src="https://alabamaveteran.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/elroy-1.png"
          alt="Chris Stricklin"
          class="ab-member-photo"
        />
        <div class="ab-member-role">Vice President</div>
        <div class="ab-member-name">Chris 'Elroy' Stricklin</div>
        <div class="ab-member-title">
          Air Force Colonel (ret) · Business Executive &amp; Speaker
        </div>
        <p class="ab-member-bio">
          A three-time bestselling author and nationally recognized keynote speaker, Elroy served 23
          years in the Air Force — from F-15C and the Thunderbirds to DARPA and the Pentagon, with
          combat tours in Iraq and Afghanistan. He is a passionate advocate for veteran mental
          health.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="ab-member">
        <img
          src="https://alabamaveteran.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/jessepic.webp"
          alt="Jesse Elders"
          class="ab-member-photo"
        />
        <div class="ab-member-role">Secretary</div>
        <div class="ab-member-name">Jesse Elders</div>
        <div class="ab-member-title">US Navy Reserves</div>
        <p class="ab-member-bio">
          An insurance and operations professional with a background in claims, Jesse is a Navy
          Seabee veteran who continues to serve in the Naval Reserves. He brings operational
          discipline and a ground-level veteran perspective to everything the organization does.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="ab-member">
        <img
          src="https://alabamaveteran.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Dylanpic.webp"
          alt="Dylan Angeline"
          class="ab-member-photo"
        />
        <div class="ab-member-role">Parliamentarian</div>
        <div class="ab-member-name">Dylan Angeline</div>
        <div class="ab-member-title">Corporate Counsel · Community Health Systems</div>
        <p class="ab-member-bio">
          An Air Force veteran and attorney specializing in business litigation and healthcare
          advisory services, Dylan has served as a senior health policy analyst in Washington, D.C.
          He also serves on the board of Dovetail Landing, supporting behavioral health services for
          veterans and their families.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="ab-member">
        <img
          src="https://alabamaveteran.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/mikepic.webp"
          alt="James Mike Oakley"
          class="ab-member-photo"
        />
        <div class="ab-member-role">Board Member</div>
        <div class="ab-member-name">James "Mike" Oakley</div>
        <div class="ab-member-title">Mayor · Centreville, AL</div>
        <p class="ab-member-bio">
          Mike served nearly 40 years in the Alabama Army National Guard, retiring as Command
          Sergeant Major — the highest enlisted rank in the U.S. Armed Forces. Elected Mayor of
          Centreville in 2020, his career spans military service, journalism, education, and public
          service at every level of Alabama government.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="ab-member">
        <img
          src="https://www.thenolesgroup.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/dannyjnoles.jpg"
          alt="Danny Noles"
          class="ab-member-photo"
        />
        <div class="ab-member-role">Board Member</div>
        <div class="ab-member-name">Danny Noles</div>
        <div class="ab-member-title">Founder &amp; CEO · The Noles Group</div>
        <p class="ab-member-bio">
          Danny grew up in Roanoke, Alabama and attended Auburn University through the ROTC program
          before serving in the United States Army. His military service shaped the discipline and
          leadership that define his 30-year career in financial services. He founded The Noles
          Group in 2016, focusing on retirement and financial planning across Alabama. A supporter
          of Alabama Veteran since day one in 2016, Danny has served on the board for three years
          and brings a deep commitment to veterans and community to the table.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="ab-board-grid-bottom">
      <div class="ab-member">
        <img
          src={`${base}assets/board/matt-schlagenhauf.webp`}
          alt="Matt Schlagenhauf"
          class="ab-member-photo"
          width="400"
          height="600"
          loading="lazy"
          decoding="async"
        />
        <div class="ab-member-role">Board Member</div>
        <div class="ab-member-name">Matt Schlagenhauf</div>
        <div class="ab-member-title">U.S. Army Veteran · Warrior Retreat Cadre</div>
        <p class="ab-member-bio">
          Matt is a U.S. Army and Alabama Army National Guard veteran who serves on the Board of
          Directors and as a Warrior Retreat Cadre. Born and raised in Decatur, Alabama, he served
          13 years in support of Operation Iraqi Freedom and Operation Enduring Freedom, with
          deployments to Iraq and Colombia, before continuing to support the warfighter as an Army
          civilian contractor specializing in simulation programs and UAS training. Honored by
          Alabama Veteran in 2017, he helped develop, implement, and grow the Warrior Retreat
          program so veterans have space to reconnect, heal, and build relationships through Post
          Traumatic Growth. The program has expanded to include retreats for couples and female
          veterans. As a board member he fosters collaboration among veteran organizations so no
          veteran faces their struggles alone. He leads with a simple mission: to create spaces
          where veterans can find strength, connection, and purpose — together.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div
        class="ab-member"
        style="
            background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.02);
            border-top-color: rgba(178, 31, 36, 0.25);
            display: flex;
            flex-direction: column;
            justify-content: center;
            align-items: center;
            text-align: center;
          "
      >
        <div
          class="ab-join-title"
          style="
              font-family: 'League Gothic', sans-serif;
              font-size: 42px;
              text-transform: uppercase;
              letter-spacing: 1px;
              margin-bottom: 10px;
            "
        >
          Join Us
        </div>
        <p class="ab-join-copy" style="font-size: 13px; max-width: 260px; line-height: 1.65">
          Interested in serving on the Alabama Veteran board? We'd love to hear from you.
        </p>
        <a
          href="mailto:c.montz@alabamaveteran.org"
          class="btn-ow ab-join-cta"
          style="margin-top: 20px; font-size: 11px; padding: 10px 24px">Get in Touch</a
        >
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
